    <div>
      <section class="rz-doc-grid" id="quick-start">
        <article class="rz-doc-card">
          <h3>1. Create an account</h3>
          <p>Go to /register, select a username, and complete the sign-up form. This username becomes part of your public profile URL such as /yourname.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="rz-doc-card">
          <h3>2. Verify and login</h3>
          <p>Check your email, confirm your account, and log in. Verification is required before many features are fully available.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="rz-doc-card">
          <h3>3. Build your page</h3>
          <p>Fill in your bio, links, profile image, banner, and visual theme. Then publish and share the final page with your audience.</p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="register-login">
        <h2>Register and login</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-steps">
          <div class="rz-step">
            <div class="rz-step-num">1</div>
            <h3>Visit the sign-up page</h3>
            <p>Open /register and create a new account. Choose a username that is short, memorable, and easy to share. This is usually the main identity used in your public showcase.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-step">
            <div class="rz-step-num">2</div>
            <h3>Confirm your email</h3>
            <p>After you submit the form, the app may send a verification note. Open the email and verify your address. This helps activate your account and makes the page usable for public sharing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-step">
            <div class="rz-step-num">3</div>
            <h3>Log in to the dashboard</h3>
            <p>Use your email or username credentials to sign in, then open the dashboard. This is the main control area where you manage your profile, links, images, theme, and visibility.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="rz-callout">
          If the verification email is not received, check spam and junk folders first. If the account still does not verify, the mail configuration likely needs to be corrected in the backend environment.
        </div>

        <div class="rz-doc-card" style="margin-top: 22px;">
          <h3>What the registration flow is meant to do</h3>
          <p>Registration creates your user identity, your showcase slug, and your profile state. Once you complete verification and login, you can use Rizzzler as a fully functional profile page with custom branding and social links.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Creates your account record</li>
            <li>Assigns your profile URL</li>
            <li>Allows dashboard customization</li>
            <li>Activates your public showcase</li>
            <li>Lets you manage privacy, media, and theme</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="dashboard">
        <h2>Dashboard tour</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-grid">
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Profile information</h3>
            <p>Use this area to update your display name, bio, role, location, and any identity details that define how visitors see your page.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Theme and style</h3>
            <p>Choose the visual appearance of your showcase. Rizzzler includes multiple themes with different moods, from bright and playful to dark, neon, and premium.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Links and contacts</h3>
            <p>Add important destinations such as Instagram, X, GitHub, portfolio, blog, email, or business profiles so visitors can reach you quickly.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Media management</h3>
            <p>Upload and manage your profile image, banner, gallery content, and custom showcase audio. You can also edit the hero eyebrow text and the text that appears under each moment block on your public page.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Privacy controls</h3>
            <p>Keep your page hidden temporarily when needed, or make it public when you are ready to share it with the world.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Account settings</h3>
            <p>Review your account status, basic user details, and public visibility preferences so your showcase stays relevant and up to date.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="auth-flow">
        <h2>How login and authentication work</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-card">
          <p>The login flow is not just a simple front-end action. It is the security layer that connects your account with your public profile, dashboard settings, and theme data.</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Create account:</strong> You register a username, email, and password.</li>
            <li><strong>Receive verification:</strong> The app checks whether your email is valid and whether your account is active.</li>
            <li><strong>Log in:</strong> After verification, you return to the login page and sign in with your credentials.</li>
            <li><strong>Session creation:</strong> The backend creates an authenticated session so your user data stays connected while you browse.</li>
            <li><strong>Dashboard access:</strong> Once logged in, you can manage your page, links, gallery, theme, visibility, and account details.</li>
            <li><strong>Public profile:</strong> Your public URL is generated from your username, and visitors can view your sharable page without logging in.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="rz-callout" style="margin-top: 18px;">
          This is the full user journey: register → verify → login → customize → save → publish → share. If any step fails, the result is usually an email issue, session issue, or environment configuration issue.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="profile-building">
        <h2>How to build a strong profile page</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-card">
          <h3>Start with the core message</h3>
          <p>Your bio should explain who you are, what you do, and why someone should click your links. A good profile does not try to say everything. It focuses on one message and makes it easy to understand.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Write in clear, human language</li>
            <li>Use a strong first sentence</li>
            <li>Keep the profile concise</li>
            <li>Focus on the type of audience you want</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rz-doc-card" style="margin-top: 20px;">
          <h3>What to include on a good page</h3>
          <p>A full profile page works best when it feels intentional. Keep each section focused and visually clean.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Profile image or brand avatar</li>
            <li>Short bio</li>
            <li>Role or niche label</li>
            <li>Primary links</li>
            <li>Gallery or showcase items</li>
            <li>Theme that matches your identity</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="all-themes">
        <h2>Theme guide: every theme in Rizzzler</h2>
        <p>These are the built-in visual styles available in the dashboard. Each one gives a different mood and is meant to fit a different kind of profile.</p>
        <div class="rz-theme-grid">
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#8ab4f8"></span><h3>Moonlight</h3></div>
            <p>Soft blue-silver tones with calm glow effects. Best for a clean, elegant, premium personal brand.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#ff4d4d"></span><h3>Scary Sky</h3></div>
            <p>Stormy, dramatic, and intense with jagged shapes and electrified mood. Best for darker or edgy identities.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#a855f7"></span><h3>Dark Nights</h3></div>
            <p>Neon synthwave style with cyber details and glowing contrast. Perfect for futuristic and tech-heavy profiles.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#ff9ab8"></span><h3>Cute Foxy</h3></div>
            <p>Pastel, playful, and bright with a scrapbook feel. Great for cute, cheerful, creative personal pages.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#ffd166"></span><h3>Diva</h3></div>
            <p>Luxury stage energy with glow, spotlight vibe, and glamorous styling. Ideal for creators and artists.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#5ee7ff"></span><h3>Scifi</h3></div>
            <p>Holographic cyber aesthetic with futuristic motion and a tech-driven identity. Best for digital-first brands.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#d78b2e"></span><h3>Rocky</h3></div>
            <p>Earthy, rugged, and grounded. This theme looks bold and cinematic, fitting strong personal brands.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#7ee8fa"></span><h3>Frostbyte</h3></div>
            <p>Cool glassy blue aesthetic with icy technical details. Great for minimal and futuristic profiles.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-theme-card">
            <div class="rz-theme-card-header"><span class="rz-theme-swatch" style="background:#ff7ad9"></span><h3>Bubble Pop</h3></div>
