      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="customization">
        <h2>Customization guide</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-grid">
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Choose a theme that matches your brand</h3>
            <p>Rizzzler has different visual styles for different identities. Pick something that matches your purpose: friendly, creative, professional, dark, or playful.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Use effects carefully</h3>
            <p>Effects and decorations can make your page more dynamic, but they should support the design rather than overpower it. One strong visual direction works better than many conflicting ones.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Keep content readable</h3>
            <p>Even if the page is visually rich, readability should remain high. Good contrast, clean spacing, and consistent fonts make your page easier to browse.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Best practice for design</h3>
            <p>Use one color story, one tone of voice, and a minimal but unique layout. This keeps your page memorable and professional.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="rz-callout">
          If a newly added theme does not appear in Customize, the usual reason is that the app is still running with an older in-memory registry. Restart the app and refresh the dashboard. The theme must also exist in the shared registry and have a matching CSS file.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="media">
        <h2>Media and uploads</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-grid">
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Profile image</h3>
            <p>Use a clear portrait, avatar, or logo. Visitors often decide in seconds whether a page feels credible, so first impressions matter.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Banner image</h3>
            <p>A banner adds depth and personality to the page. It should support the theme and feel aligned with the rest of the content.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Gallery and showcase content</h3>
            <p>Display your strongest work, projects, or photos in a clean arrangement. A simple gallery is often more effective than a crowded one.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Audio settings</h3>
            <p>Audio can create mood, but it should be used carefully. Keep it tasteful and make sure it does not overwhelm the content. You can choose a preset track or upload your own audio file from the dashboard; user uploads are capped below 1MB and are stored in MongoDB.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="rz-doc-card" style="margin-top: 22px;">
          <h3>Upload tips</h3>
          <p>For best results, use optimized media sizes and standard formats. Large files may slow down the page or fail to upload completely. Always keep the final page fast and clean.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Use compressed images when possible</li>
            <li>Keep banner and gallery visuals high quality but lightweight</li>
            <li>Use supported formats for uploaded audio: MP3, WAV, OGG, M4A, AAC, MP4, WEBA, and WEBM</li>
            <li>Custom uploaded audio must stay under 1MB and is automatically cleaned up if it is removed or left orphaned</li>
            <li>Keep important content readable on mobile devices</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="visibility">
        <h2>Privacy, visibility, and page control</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-grid">
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Public by default</h3>
            <p>Once your account is active and verified, your showcase should generally be visible at your public username URL.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Temporary hiding</h3>
            <p>If you are editing your page or want a private period, you can hide it from the dashboard while keeping your account in place.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="rz-doc-card">
            <h3>Revision-friendly</h3>
            <p>You can update the page as often as needed without resetting your entire identity. This makes it easy to keep your profile fresh and relevant.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="seo">
        <h2>SEO and sharing tips</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-card">
          <p>Your Rizzzler profile is more discoverable when it has a clear username, good content, and strong metadata. Use a clean title, strong bio, and share your public URL across relevant platforms.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Use a memorable username</li>
            <li>Keep your bio targeted and keyword friendly</li>
            <li>Share the profile on social channels and communities</li>
            <li>Use your public link consistently across your online presence</li>
            <li>Keep your page updated so visitors see current work and contact information</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="troubleshooting">
        <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
        <div class="rz-troubleshoot-grid">
          <div class="rz-troubleshoot-item">
            <h3>Theme missing from Customize</h3>
            <p>Restart the server. Make sure the theme exists in the shared registry and that it has a matching CSS file in public/css/themes. This is the most common reason a new style fails to appear.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-troubleshoot-item">
            <h3>Verification email not arriving</h3>
            <p>Check your spam or junk folder. If it still does not arrive, validate your mail credentials, SMTP host, and any app environment values that control email delivery.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-troubleshoot-item">
            <h3>Profile is hidden or not loading</h3>
            <p>Check whether the account is active and whether the page has been paused or hidden in settings. Refresh the page after any visibility change.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-troubleshoot-item">
            <h3>Image upload failed</h3>
            <p>Try a smaller file, a supported format, and a cleaner image. Some unsupported types or very large files are rejected by the server.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-troubleshoot-item">
            <h3>Dashboard changes are not saving</h3>
            <p>Review the values you are submitting and ensure they match expected formats. Bad theme keys, invalid media references, or unsupported values can stop a save from working.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-troubleshoot-item">
            <h3>Login is not working</h3>
            <p>Verify the account exists, the password is correct, and the app session config is running properly. If the issue persists, clear cookies and retry.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-troubleshoot-item">
            <h3>Public page looks outdated</h3>
            <p>Open the dashboard and confirm the latest content has saved. Sometimes the page is correct but the browser is still showing a cached version.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rz-troubleshoot-item">
            <h3>Need to restart in development</h3>
            <p>When new theme files or setting changes are added, restart the app so the latest routes, templates, and registry data are reloaded.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="error-fixes">
        <h2>Common errors and fixes</h2>
        <div class="rz-doc-card">
          <table class="rz-error-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Problem</th>
                <th>Why it happens</th>
                <th>How to fix it</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>New theme not showing in Customize</td>
                <td>The server is still running an older theme list or the theme key is missing from the registry</td>
                <td>Restart the app and confirm the theme is added in the shared registry and CSS file exists</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Verification email not received</td>
                <td>SMTP is not configured correctly or the email was filtered into spam</td>
                <td>Check the mail settings, spam folder, and server environment values before retrying</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Login page keeps rejecting credentials</td>
                <td>Password is wrong, the account is not active, or the session is broken</td>
                <td>Verify the account, reset the password if needed, and clear cookies before trying again</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Image upload fails</td>
                <td>Unsupported format, too large a file, or incorrect upload handling</td>
                <td>Use a smaller supported image and confirm the server accepts the file type</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Profile page looks outdated</td>
                <td>The browser is caching older content or the latest save did not complete</td>
                <td>Refresh the page, clear cache if necessary, and confirm your dashboard changes saved</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Profile is hidden</td>
                <td>Visibility settings were turned off or account is still unverified</td>
                <td>Open dashboard settings and enable visibility again, then verify the account status</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-panel" id="faq">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <div class="rz-faq-list">
          <% faqItems.forEach((item) => { %>
            <div class="rz-faq-item">
              <h3><%= item.q %></h3>
              <p><%= item.a %></p>
            </div>
          <% }) %>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rz-doc-cta">
        <h3>Ready to build your Rizzzler page?</h3>
        <div class="rz-doc-actions">
          <a class="rz-doc-button rz-doc-button-primary" href="/register">Create account</a>
          <a class="rz-doc-button rz-doc-button-secondary" href="/login">Login to dashboard</a>
          <a class="rz-doc-button rz-doc-button-secondary" href="/dashboard/settings">Open settings</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
